{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #704: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $G_n$ be the unit distance graph in $\\mathbb{R}^n$, with two vertices joined by an edge if and only if the distance between them is $1$.\n\nEstimate the chromatic number $\\chi(G_n)$. Does it grow exponentially in $n$? Does\\[\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\chi(G_n)^{1/n}\\]exist? Current best: Prosanov \\cite{Pr20} has given an alternative proof of this upper bound. [Pr20] Prosanov, Roman, A new proof of the Larman-Rogers upper bound for the chromatic number of the Euclidean space. Prize: no. Tags: chromatic number, geometry, graph theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_38d456716620bf4623a75dd3ccb01450bc1bb168a6eb3a1981fd8c5edf8ce864","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:704","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_645e4ce8be21372e","object_root":"sha256:779e9c3b0da88c7ba3de14bdbae980f27990a653f09f232f6ba4e2ef178ae9ad","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdo